# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules, read from the site root.
#
# The mirror writes every page as a directory document (product/x/index.html), which
# Pages serves at /product/x/. That leaves the physical /index.html path reachable
# too, so the same content would have two URLs. Only the root case is fixed by hand
# here, because it is the one rule Pages cannot infer from a wildcard.
#
# The earlier version of this file listed /records/, /items/ and /about/ - routes of
# a build that no longer exists. Rules for paths a mirror does not produce are not
# harmless: they read as intent, and the next person edits the wrong thing.

/index.html    /    308

# Deep duplicates (/product/x/index.html) are handled by Pages' own trailing-slash
# and directory-index behaviour. Verify on the deployed preview before adding rules
# here: Cloudflare's handling of that case is a project setting, not something this
# file can express portably, and a speculative wildcard would either do nothing or
# rewrite asset paths that legitimately end in a filename.
#
# If Search Console later reports /…/index.html duplicates, the fix is the Pages
# setting "Project -> Build & deploy -> Trailing slash", not a line here.

# To send an old site's URLs here, one line each:
# /old-page          /            301
